# Styling Guidelines

## Tailwind CSS
- Use Tailwind classes for all styling
- Use `cn()` utility from `/src/lib/utils.ts` for conditional classes
- Follow mobile-first responsive design (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`, `2xl:`)
- Use Tailwind's spacing scale (4px increments: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, etc.)
- Prefer Tailwind utilities over custom CSS when possible

Example:
```typescript
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"

export function Card({ className, isActive }: CardProps) {
  return (
    <div
      className={cn(
        "rounded-lg border bg-card p-6",
        "hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow",
        isActive && "ring-2 ring-primary",
        className
      )}
    >
      {/* content */}
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Responsive Design
- Use mobile-first approach (base styles for mobile, then add breakpoints)
- Standard breakpoints: `sm` (640px), `md` (768px), `lg` (1024px), `xl` (1280px), `2xl` (1536px)
- Test on multiple screen sizes
- Consider touch targets (minimum 44x44px for interactive elements)

Example:
```typescript
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
  {/* cards */}
</div>
```

## Theme Support
- Use `next-themes` for dark mode
- Define colors in CSS variables (configured in `app.css`)
- Use semantic color names (e.g., `bg-background`, `text-foreground`)
- Test both light and dark modes
- Respect system preference

Example:
```typescript
// Use semantic colors
<div className="bg-background text-foreground">
  <h1 className="text-primary">Title</h1>
  <p className="text-muted-foreground">Description</p>
</div>
```

## CSS Variables
- Theme colors defined in `app.css`:
  - `--background`, `--foreground`
  - `--primary`, `--primary-foreground`
  - `--secondary`, `--secondary-foreground`
  - `--muted`, `--muted-foreground`
  - `--accent`, `--accent-foreground`
  - `--destructive`, `--destructive-foreground`
  - `--border`, `--input`, `--ring`
  - `--radius`

## Spacing
- Use consistent spacing throughout the app
- Common spacing values: 2, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32
- Use `space-y-*` for vertical spacing between elements
- Use `gap-*` for grid/flex gaps

Example:
```typescript
<div className="space-y-4">
  <div>Item 1</div>
  <div>Item 2</div>
  <div>Item 3</div>
</div>
```

## Typography
- Font family defined in root layout (Geist Sans, Geist Mono)
- Use semantic heading tags: `h1`, `h2`, `h3`, etc.
- Use Tailwind text utilities: `text-sm`, `text-base`, `text-lg`, `text-xl`, etc.
- Line height: `leading-tight`, `leading-normal`, `leading-relaxed`

Example:
```typescript
<div>
  <h1 className="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Main Title</h1>
  <h2 className="text-2xl font-semibold">Section Title</h2>
  <p className="text-base text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
    Body text
  </p>
</div>
```

## Animations
- Use `tw-animate-css` for animations
- Keep animations subtle and purposeful
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Common animations: fade-in, slide-up, pulse, spin

Example:
```typescript
<div className="animate-fade-in">
  {/* content */}
</div>

<button className="hover:animate-pulse">
  Click me
</button>
```

## Layout Patterns
- Use flexbox for one-dimensional layouts
- Use grid for two-dimensional layouts
- Use container for content width constraints
- Use fixed positioning sparingly

Example:
```typescript
// Flex layout
<div className="flex items-center justify-between">
  <div>Left</div>
  <div>Right</div>
</div>

// Grid layout
<div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  <div>1</div>
  <div>2</div>
  <div>3</div>
</div>

// Container
<div className="container mx-auto px-4">
  {/* content */}
</div>
```

## Component Styling Patterns

### Card Pattern
```typescript
<div className="rounded-lg border bg-card p-6 shadow-sm">
  <h3 className="font-semibold">Card Title</h3>
  <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Card content</p>
</div>
```

### Button Variants (use shadcn/ui Button)
```typescript
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"

<Button variant="default">Primary</Button>
<Button variant="secondary">Secondary</Button>
<Button variant="outline">Outline</Button>
<Button variant="ghost">Ghost</Button>
<Button variant="destructive">Delete</Button>
```

### Form Styling
```typescript
<div className="space-y-4">
  <div className="space-y-2">
    <label className="text-sm font-medium">Label</label>
    <input
      type="text"
      className="w-full rounded-md border border-input bg-background px-3 py-2"
    />
  </div>
</div>
```

## Accessibility
- Maintain color contrast ratios (WCAG AA minimum)
- Use focus indicators (ring classes)
- Test keyboard navigation
- Provide visual feedback for interactive elements

Example:
```typescript
<button className="focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary focus:ring-offset-2">
  Accessible button
</button>
```

## Custom CSS
- Avoid custom CSS when possible (use Tailwind first)
- If custom CSS is needed, use CSS modules or styled components
- Document why Tailwind couldn't be used
- Keep custom styles co-located with components

## Performance
- Purge unused styles (configured in tailwind.config)
- Use JIT mode (enabled by default in Tailwind 4)
- Avoid deeply nested @apply directives
- Consider bundle size when adding custom animations
